    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 16 right parenthesis squared equals 289\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>289</mn>\n</mrow></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the given equation is a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane. The point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis q comma s right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the circle. Which of the following is NOT a possible value of <math alttext=\"q\"><mi>q</mi></math>?</p>",
