    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math>. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written in the form <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math alttext=\"left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the center of the circle and <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the radius of the circle. It's given that the circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane is defined by <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 3 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 289\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>289</mn></math>. Therefore, <math alttext=\"r squared equals 289\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>289</mn></math>. Taking the positive square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"r equals 17\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>. Thus, the radius of the circle is <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math>.</p>"
