    "subtopicId": "circles",
    "subtopic": "Circles & coordinate equations",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Circle A shown is defined by the equation <math alttext=\"x squared plus left parenthesis y minus 6 right parenthesis squared equals 7\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. Circle B (not shown) has the same radius but is translated <math alttext=\"96\"><mn>96</mn></math> units to the right. If the equation of circle B is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals a\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, and <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> are constants, what is the value of <math alttext=\"4 a\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>a</mi>\n</mrow></math>?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": "28",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math>. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus t right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus s right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis t comma s right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that circle A is defined by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared plus left parenthesis y minus 6 right parenthesis squared equals 7\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, which can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 0 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 6 right parenthesis squared equals left parenthesis StartRoot 7 EndRoot right parenthesis squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals StartRoot 7 EndRoot\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math> and the radius of circle A is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartRoot 7 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that circle B has the same radius as circle A. If the equation of circle B is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals a\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals r squared\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartRoot 7 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals left parenthesis StartRoot 7 EndRoot right parenthesis squared\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals 7\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. It follows that the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 a\"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis\"><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math>.</p>",
